    </array>
    <array name="weight_bfs_wifi_help_tips">
        <item>· Place the scale as close as possible to the router to ensure a strong Wi-Fi signal</item>
        <item>· Confirm whether the input password for the Wi-Fi connection is correct.</item>
        <item>· Connect your phone to the target Wi-Fi router, and then try opening a web page to check whether you can access the Internet.</item>
        <item>· If 2.4GHz is disabled, enable and select it. The scale does not support 5GHz Wi-Fi. \n· If dual band is enabled, disable it to avoid configuration failure because of the 5GHz network.</item>
        <item>· If the Wi-Fi router is connected to the Internet, the Wi-Fi signal is strong, and the router is working with 2.4GHz enabled and dual band disabled, try restarting the router.</item>
        <item>· If restarting the router does not work, try restarting the phone.</item>
        <item>· If restarting the router does not work, try reinstalling the battery.</item>
    </array>
    <array name="weight_bfs_wifi_help_title">
        <item>1. Is the scale located in a place with strong Wi-Fi signal?</item>
        <item>2. Is the Wi-Fi password correct?</item>
        <item>3. Is the Wi-Fi router properly connected to the Internet?</item>
        <item>4. Is 2.4GHz Wi-Fi disabled on the router? Or is dual band Wi-Fi enabled?</item>
        <item>5. Try restarting the router.</item>
        <item>6. Try restarting the phone.</item>
        <item>7. Try restarting the device.</item>
    </array>
    <array name="weight_bfs_wifi_set_help_tips">
        <item>2.4 GHz Wi-Fi indicates that the wireless router operates at 2.4 GHz.\n5 GHz Wi-Fi indicates that the wireless router operates at 5 GHz.</item>
        <item>Set up your router according to the following steps:\n1. Enter the login address of your router in the address bar of your browser and log in to the background of the wireless router. \n2. Find the setting button of the wireless router. \n3. Turn off the dual band button. \n4. Enable the 2.4 GHz Wi-Fi.</item>
        <item>The following two methods can be used to check the Wi-Fi band:\n1. In the Wi-Fi list on your computer, select [Wi-Fi] &amp;gt; [Property] &amp;gt; [Network Band]. \n2. Log in to the router background.</item>
    </array>
